   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>Encapsulation of an ErrorDomain. An ErrorDomain is the controlling entity for ErrorCode’s error code values, and defines the mapping of such error code values to textual representations. This type constitutes a base class for ErrorDomain implementations. This class is a literal type, and subclasses are strongly advised to be literal types as well.</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
